title: Remus Stealer Gmail Extension — Exfiltration to prem1um.onl
id: 4f0e2b71-8d3c-4a5e-9c1d-7b62e0a91f34
status: experimental
description: Detects browser or proxy traffic to prem1um.onl, the collector endpoint the Remus Stealer Google Sheets Chrome extension POSTs stolen Gmail sender, subject, body and mailbox data to (path /m, campaign ID d7e027cf1c9989bd45ceeb3429e49cf5). The extension is unpacked into the victim's Chrome profile and registered by editing Secure Preferences, so the executable can exit while collection continues.
references:
  - https://x.com/InvokeReversing/status/2125264524995645745
  - https://malware.news/t/remus-stealer-uses-a-fake-google-sheets-extension-to-steal-gmail-messages/127620#post_1
  - https://www.hudsonrock.com/blog/remus-stealer-markets-persistent-gmail-access-hudson-rock-investigates
  - https://www.malwarebytes.com/blog/news/2026/11/remus-malware-claims-gmail-access-even-after-you-change-your-password
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/25
tags:
  - attack.t1176
  - attack.t1114
  - attack.t1041
logsource:
  category: proxy
detection:
  selection_host:
    cs-host|endswith: 'prem1um.onl'
  condition: selection_host
falsepositives:
  - Unlikely — dedicated stealer collection host with no legitimate use
level: high
